# Excludes internal repo metadata from the Cloudflare Workers static-assets bundle.
# assets.directory in wrangler.jsonc is "." (repo root), so without this the build
# tries to upload .git itself as a servable asset -- including .git/objects/pack/*.pack,
# which grows past Workers' 25 MiB per-file limit as the repo picks up real commits and
# fails the entire deploy. None of this is ever meant to be served to a visitor anyway.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
wrangler.jsonc
wrangler.staging.jsonc
.assetsignore
*.md
sql
Articles

# Business/working documents that live in the repo root but are NOT part of the
# site. assets.directory is "." and reads the FILESYSTEM, not git -- so untracked
# files here would be uploaded and served publicly by any local `wrangler deploy`
# or `wrangler versions upload`, even though Workers Builds (which builds from a
# clean clone) never sees them. That includes financial and internal planning
# documents. No page references a local file of these types.
*.pdf
*.xlsx
*.xlsb
*.docx
*.csv

# Internal working HTML that must not be served. Unlike the document types above
# these cannot be excluded by extension -- *.html IS the site -- so they are named
# individually. Keeps a local `wrangler deploy` (which reads the filesystem, not
# git) from publishing them even though they are gitignored.
domain-checklist.html
kerph-plan-comparison.html
overnight-report-*.html
shop-jigs-script.html

# Test tooling. assets.directory is "." and reads the FILESYSTEM, so without these a local
# `wrangler deploy` run after an `npm install` would upload the whole of node_modules to the
# live site. Workers Builds never sees them (clean clone + gitignored), but a local deploy
# would, which is exactly how four internal documents reached production on 2026-09-01.
node_modules
playwright-report
test-results
blob-report
package.json
package-lock.json
playwright.config.js
tests

# Repo tooling, not site content. assets.directory is "." so anything here would
# otherwise be served at kerphplans.com/scripts/.
scripts
